/.gradle-home
/.gradle
/build
/.kotlin
# Gradle's IDE-style output directory. Not produced by `gradle build` itself
# — the Kotlin plugin's IDE integration writes it — which is why it went
# unnoticed: it appeared only once a test actually ran this sample. It
# duplicates tracked source (`src/main/kotlin/Main.kt` verbatim), so
# committing it would be committing a second, silently-stale copy.
/bin
# `nix build` against this sample's flake.nix leaves a symlink into the nix
# store. Committing one records this machine's store path as if it were
# source.
/result
/result-*
